Article 5 (Assistance to Promote Use of Electronic Signatures)
The Minister of Science and ICT may provide administrative, financial and technical assistance in respect of the following in order to promote the use of electronic signatures:
Research and development, utilization and standardization of technologies related to electronic signatures;
Training of professional personnel related to electronic signatures;
Conduct of pilot projects to promote the wide use of various electronic-signature-creation devices;
Technical assistance to promote the interoperability of electronic signatures and operation of interlinking devices;
Conduct of business affairs by, and operation of, the accreditation agency designated under Article 9 and assessment bodies selected under Article 10 ;
Other matters necessary to promote the use of electronic signatures.

