Article 12 (Revocation of Selection as Assessment Body)
The Minister of Science and ICT may revoke a selection as an assessment body or may order an assessment body to suspend its business, in whole or in part, for a specified period not to exceed one year if any of the following is applicable to the assessment body: Provided , That the Minister shall revoke a selection in the case of subparagraph 1 or 2:
If the assessment body has obtained a selection by fraud or other improper means;
If the assessment body conducts an assessment during the suspension period;
If the assessment body fails to conduct an assessment without good cause;
If the assessment body fails to comply with the selection criteria under Article 10 (5);
If the assessment body conducts an assessment in violation of the code of conduct or the standards and procedures for assessment of compliance under Article 10 (5).
The Minister of Science and ICT shall hold a hearing to revoke a selection under paragraph (1).
Revocation of selections and suspension of business under paragraph (1) and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

